3 Method
3.2 Cell Representation Learning & Language Generation with Pre-Trained Models
Text LLM for Text Generation. For the text LLM, we utilize LLaMA-2 7B [47], a decoder-only transformer that excels at text generation. Its extensive pre-training and generative architecture make it well-suited for biomedical text understanding and generation, such as describing cellular states. We tokenize the textual description of cells into a sequence of tokens t ( i ) = [ t ( i ) 1 , t ( i ) 2 , . . . , t ( i ) T ] using the tokenizer in text LLM.

