3 Method
3.3 Comprehensive Cell-Text Alignment
Building upon the pre-trained models, we achieve comprehensive cell-text alignment in scMMGPT via (1) bidirectional projectors and (2) a two-stage cross-modal pre-training strategy.

--- CHUNK 17 ---
3 Method
3.3 Comprehensive Cell-Text Alignment
3.3.1 Bidirectional Projectors for Cell-Text Integration
To bridge the modality gap between cell and text LLMs, we introduce bidirectional cell-to-text and text-to-cell projectors that enable effective cross-modal alignment and information exchange.
- The cell-to-text projector is implemented with a Query Transformer (Q-Former) [33] with 32 learnable queries, which maps high-dimensional cell embeddings from the scLLM into the token embedding space of the Text LLM. We initialize the Q-Former with weights from BiomedBERT [48], a BERT encoder trained on PubMed abstracts and biomedical literature [49].
- The text-to-cell projector is realized using a stack of cross-attention layers [5] that project LLaMA-2 output embeddings into the hidden space of scGPT. The resulting representations are used as soft prompts [50], conditioning the scLLM for text-to-cell generation.
