ChatNT [13] fine-tunes the DNA encoder jointly with the projection layer, but does not assess whether pretrained biological representations contribute to performance or whether the system learns taskspecific features end-to-end. TxGemma [1], BioT5 [2], and Galactica [3] operate on text-serialized biological inputs, but discards the rich geometric and functional representations learned by specialized biological FMs. Agentic systems such as GeneGPT [26] equip LLMs with database retrieval at inference time, but can only surface information already in existing knowledge bases.

